4. Data Structure 1: In-Memory 3D Static Matrix Indexing
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
4.1 Dimensional Coordinates & Index Mapping Math
[City][BloodGroup][MaxHeap]
To achieve true constant-time retrieval of voluntary blood donors across 34 Gujarat districts without disk I/O or
database table scanning, the system implements an in-memory Three-Dimensional Static Array Matrix:
donors[City][BloodGroup] = new MaxHeap().
The mathematical coordinates are defined by static, bijection hash mappings:
• Dimension 1 (City Axis $C$): Maps each recognized Gujarat district or city to a primary key in memory (e.g.,
Ahmedabad, Gandhinagar, Surat, Vadodara, Rajkot, Kutch, etc.).
• Dimension 2 (Blood Group Axis $G$, Size = 8): Maps ABO/Rh serological phenotypes: O-, O+, A-, A+, B-, B+, AB-,
AB+.
• Dimension 3 (Binary Max-Heap Leaf $H$): An active instance of MaxHeap that manages the priority queue of all
verified, active donors belonging to that specific city and blood group cell.
// Core 3D Matrix Implementation (src/core/data_structures/3D_Array_Donor.js)
class DonorManager {
constructor() {
// 3D Array Matrix Structure:
// this.donors[City][BloodGroup] = new MaxHeap()
this.donors = {};
}
async init_donor_3D_array() {
const pool = getPool();
const [rows] = await pool.query(`
SELECT id, name, phone, email, age, weight, city, blood_group, is_first_time, preferred_slot
FROM donors WHERE is_active = 1
`);
this.donors = {};
for (const row of rows) {
const city = row.city;
const bg = row.blood_group;
if (!this.donors[city]) this.donors[city] = {};
if (!this.donors[city][bg]) this.donors[city][bg] = new MaxHeap();
const priority = (row.is_first_time ? 60 : 30) + Math.max(10, 40 - Math.abs((row.age || 25) - 25));
this.donors[city][bg].insert(formatDonor(row, priority));
}
return this.donors;
}
}
4.2 Constant-Time O(1) Insertion & Compatibility Retrieval Invariants
The 3D static matrix guarantees mathematical determinism across all donor transactions:
▪ O(1) Cell Indexing Invariant: Accessing any donor pool executes in strict $O(1)$ constant time via const heap =
this.donors[city]?.[bloodGroup]. No search loops, B-tree disk traversals, or string searches are executed.
